\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. And didst Thou love the race that loved not Thee?
\par And didst Thou take to heaven a human brow?
\par Dost plead with man's voice by the marvelous sea
\par Art Thou his kinsman now?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O God, O kinsman, loved, but not enough
\par O Man, with eyes majestic after death
\par Whose feet have toiled along our pathways rough,
\par Whose lips drawn human breath!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. By that one likeness which doth 
\par hold us kin,
\par By that high heaven where, sinless Thou dost shine,
\par To draw us sinners in;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. By Thy last silence in the judgement hall,
\par By long foreknowledge of the deadly tree,
\par By darkness, by the wormwood and the gall,
\par I pray Thee visit me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Come, lest this heart should, cold and cast away,
\par Die ere the Guest adored she entertain
\par Lest eyes that never saw Thine earthly day
\par Should miss Thy heavenly reign.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

